Feature follow-up (unreleased; base v1.4.5):
- [FIXED] PR review: preserve normal POSIX permissions on separate outputs,
    use exclusive rename/link/copy publication across filesystem capabilities,
    and keep zero DC offset display consistent with v1.4.5 (no negative zero).
- [IMPLEMENTED] Separate --output / --output-dir with no-clobber publication
    and relative recursive layout; originals are retained.
- [IMPLEMENTED] DC-corrected true-peak measurement/ceiling and verification
    of actual quantized output before publication.
- [IMPLEMENTED] Exact-block BS.1770 integrated LUFS with pooled album gating,
    explicit targets and manual-only treatment of below-gate material.
- [IMPLEMENTED] 176.4/192 kHz input: analysis-only FIR decimation for legacy
    ReplayGain; source-rate LUFS/true peak; unchanged output rate/frame count.
- [IMPLEMENTED] Optional rate-aware TPDF/first-order dither family; existing
    F44 family remains the default. Listening evaluation remains open.
- [IMPLEMENTED] R128Net-inspired C kernel optimizations with native reference
    equality tests. Details: doc/loudness-implementation.md.
- [IMPLEMENTED] Further native improvements: expression-preserving stereo
    block-energy SIMD and a peak-only adapter bypass for loudness filtering.
    Three-way reference/previous/current equality and CPU benchmarks recorded.
- [OPEN] Native Windows validation for new output paths and measurement modes.
- [OPEN] Evaluate additional R128Net screening/dense-loop optimizations using
    the reference equality gate; synthetic CPU benchmarks are not end-to-end
    throughput claims. No .NET runtime dependency is introduced.

Safety review follow-up: 2026-10-16 (base commit ef3efeb).
Report: doc/code-review-2026-10-16.md
Reproduce: make check; make check-sanitize; make check-interop

- [DONE] R1/R7: validate RIFF chunk boundaries before editing headers;
    preserve marker-like metadata and rebuild odd-length data padding.
- [DONE] R2/R3/R5: bounded AIFF/AIFC header parsing, mono/stereo 16-bit
    validation, and fresh WAV headers for AIFF-to-WAV conversions.
- [DONE] R4: stream formatted logs without a fixed-size message buffer;
    reject log filenames that exceed the path buffer.
- [DONE] R8/R9: validate WAV gain payloads and finite positive scales;
    decode binary64 without exponent shifts; reconstruct signed PCM through
    unsigned arithmetic; preserve quantizer bits using memcpy.
- [DONE] R10/R11: propagate metadata/header/seek/finalization failures,
    clean up allocation failures, preserve originals and report failed batches
    with a nonzero status. Fault injection and CLI regressions cover these.
- [IMPLEMENTED, VALIDATION OPEN] R6: exclusive Windows temporary creation
    and replacement via MoveFileExA without pre-deleting the original.
    Native Windows success, locked-file/permission failures and path tests
    are still required.
- [DONE] Serialize clean/build for debug/release/asan under parallel make;
    include UBSan and add make check-sanitize. Restore working directories
    on traversal errors and avoid recursive POSIX directory symlink cycles.
- [FOLLOW-UP ABOVE] Sound-quality extensions: the optional rate dither,
    true-peak/headroom and output-peak measurement are implemented in the
    unreleased feature branch. Ordinary legacy output remains unchanged.
- [OPEN] Encapsulate analysis/dither globals before library or parallel use.
    The existing non-UTF-8 license comment is unchanged; Clang's debug build
    still reports its encoding warning. License-header cleanup remains open.

Implementation follow-up: 2026-10-14 (base commit 8b224d3).
Details: doc/todo-fixes.txt
Historical investigation: doc/todo-investigation.txt / .json
Current probe results: doc/todo-fixed.json
Reproduce: make check; make check-interop (requires FFmpeg)

- [DONE] Native 64-bit audio corruption / forced -m32 build.
    Fixed in 8b224d3: fixed-width PCM, portable lrint, native builds,
    large-file offsets and fast-mode positions. PCM and large-file checks
    cover the fix, including sparse Wave64 input/output above 4 GiB.

- [DONE] Percentages sometimes show > 100% done (or inf%).
    Progress uses processed frames per file and planned per-file durations
    overall. Short/fractional durations, mixed sample rates, skipped files,
    Undo and empty audio are covered. Successful writes finish at 100%.

- [DONE] ReplayGain / manual gain / DC correction / clipping.
    Channel extrema and actual frame counts determine peaks after the
    selected track/album DC correction. Gain caps use corrected peaks;
    album caps are selected after all track means are known. Manual gain
    is added once. The limiter retains its existing cap unless --noclip
    is used. New Peak is documented as the pre-limiter prediction.
    Regression coverage includes asymmetric PCM/float, distinct album
    means, manual gain, no-offset, limiter and unshaped dither.

- [DONE] --help layout, wildcard instructions, man/HTML sync.
    doc/help.json generates CLI text, README help, nroff and HTML via
    make docs. make check-docs rejects stale files and undocumented options.
    Build/platform conditions, Wave64, byte-based fast thresholds, quoting,
    case sensitivity and peak/limiter semantics are retained or clarified.
    Runtime checks covered macOS arm64/x86_64 and Linux x86_64; a MinGW-w64
    build was checked under Wine. Native Windows runtime checks remain a
    portability follow-up.
- [OPEN] The 'gain' chunk scale is big-endian on macOS (__APPLE__) and
    little-endian elsewhere, so -w files are not portable across them.

- [OPEN] Standard license/copyright headers in all sources.
    Deferred to a separate change: source license notices are unchanged
    here. Findings are in doc/todo-investigation.txt.

Performance investigation (2026-10-14): doc/conversion-performance.txt
- [DONE] Paired stereo ReplayGain filters: expression-preserving SIMD on
    Clang and GCC 5+ for AArch64 and x86_64, with FP contraction disabled in
    the filters so scalar and paired paths are bitwise identical.
    Mono and other targets retain scalar/legacy paths.
    Use make verified-release (VERIFY_SIMD=auto|1|0) to require runtime
    equality before installation.
    Kernel/API state, histogram boundaries and unaffected-rate output
    match the scalar reference bit-for-bit on tested builds. Current benchmark
    gives ~1.5x ordinary stereo conversion throughput on macOS arm64.
    Details and limits: doc/filter-simd-investigation.txt.
- [DONE] IEEE float serializer: replace frexp/byte reconstruction with guarded
    binary32 bit copying and an explicit little-endian fallback. Subnormals
    retain their value; signed zeros still serialize as positive zero.
    Exact-byte edge tests and input immutability checks cover the serializer.
- [DONE] 88.2kHz ReplayGain: both old denominators were unstable (real poles
    ~1.426 and ~1.067). Replace only this rate with FFmpeg coefficients in both
    table layouts; all twelve rates pass stability checks. Reject non-finite
    RMS levels and clamp before histogram casts. FFmpeg comparison and
    mono/stereo WAV/Wave64 conversion/undo checks cover the corrected rate.
- [DONE] Legacy SSE2 Yule kernel used padding instead of b10. Correct its
    final numerator tap; all-rate impulse/DC/tone checks against long-double
    reference pass under x86_64 Clang. Native Windows/MSVC execution remains
    a platform validation follow-up.
- [DONE] Reuse conversion/packing buffers per output file; check allocation,
    byte-count overflow and write failures before replacing the original file.
    Buffer reuse preserves integer packing and gain/dither/RNG arithmetic.
    See doc/conversion-safe-implementation.txt and conversion-safe-performance.json.
    Overall speed differences remain small in the 96 kHz synthetic benchmark.
- [OPEN] Profile noise-shaped dither and common-path specialization separately;
    preserve RNG/history/rounding semantics. Compiler flags alone gave only
    modest or inconsistent gains in this workload.
